# Browser
# Faithless Looting has flashback {2}{R} printed on it, and Stingcaster Mage's trigger gives its card in the graveyard
# flashback "until end of turn. The flashback cost is equal to its mana cost" (CR 702.34a): two ways to cast it from there, which
# Bot1's page offers as the rows of the card's menu. Each row names its own flashback cost - "Flashback {2}{R}" and
# "Flashback {R}" - where the granted one read only "Cast Faithless Looting", the same as having no way at all. Bot1 casts the
# card with the granted flashback, paying {R} out of what Black Lotus left, and the card is exiled instead of going back.

